**Open questions recorded rather than decided:**
- Who names the legacy frontend id (owner, per F2).
- The registry-prefix shadowing is only inferred and needs a failing test first.
- `yang.antlr.packet` emits a Python-named diagnostic, which would mislabel errors for a second ANTLR language.

**Choices you may want to check:**
- **Ruling 4:** I used the cross-ruling's wording, which corrects the design. Module names are derivable from rows, but their manifest addresses also need the pinned resolution snapshot, so I did not keep the design's "no new manifest key" claim.
- **Address stability:** I kept the existing 8.5.3 note that "every bundled unit's address changes" when the prelude grows. It is still true of the bundled profile. The design said this ends under linking; the cross-ruling narrows that to the code root only, since the manifest still changes.
- **Ordering paragraph:** it names C2-S2 and safepoint slice 2 as "in flight at design time". C2-S2 has since landed (`c3f2da8f`), so I kept the design's sequence without claiming they are all still pending.
